<MafiaLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="How Mafia for iPhone handles local player photos, purchases, subscriptions and support messages.">
  <p class="eyebrow">Mafia for iPhone</p><h1>Privacy Policy</h1><p class="updated">Last updated: October 7, 2026</p>
  <p>This policy describes how Bubble App Studio handles information when you use Mafia for iPhone (bundle ID: bubble.app.studio.mafia) and these support pages.</p>
  <h2>Who is responsible?</h2><p>Bubble App Studio is responsible for the processing described here. For privacy questions or requests, email <a class="contact" href="mailto:contact@bubbleappstudio.xyz?subject=mafia%20ios%20app">contact@bubbleappstudio.xyz</a>.</p>
  <h2>Your game stays on your device</h2><p>Mafia does not require an account. Player names, optional player photos and game state are used locally on your device. The app does not upload these names or photos to Bubble App Studio or RevenueCat, and does not use photos for face recognition. Camera access is optional and can be changed in iOS Settings.</p><p>Game narration and sound effects are bundled with the app. The app does not record your conversations or send microphone recordings to an audio provider.</p>
  <h2>Purchases and subscriptions</h2><p>Apple processes payments. We use RevenueCat to validate purchases, restore access, manage Premium entitlements and understand subscription performance. This involves purchase history, product and transaction identifiers, subscription status, a randomly generated app user identifier and technical information such as app and operating system versions. We do not provide RevenueCat with your player names, photos or email address.</p><p>We do not receive your full payment card details. See <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/">Apple’s privacy information</a> and <a href="https://www.revenuecat.com/privacy">RevenueCat’s privacy information</a> for more about these providers.</p>
  <h2>No advertising tracking</h2><p>Mafia contains no ads. We do not sell personal information or share it for cross-app targeted advertising. The app does not integrate Firebase, AppsFlyer or Amplitude. Subscription analytics are provided through RevenueCat.</p>
  <h2>When you contact us</h2><p>If you email us, we receive your email address, message and any attachments you choose to send. We use them to answer your request and troubleshoot the issue. Please avoid sending unnecessary personal information.</p>
  <h2>These web pages</h2><p>These pages are hosted on GitHub Pages. The hosting provider may process connection information, such as your IP address and browser request details, to deliver and secure the website. We do not add advertising pixels or analytics cookies to the Mafia pages. External services linked from these pages have their own privacy policies.</p>
  <h2>Why we process information</h2><p>Where applicable under data protection law, we rely on performance of our contract to provide purchased features and support; legitimate interests to maintain the service, prevent fraud and understand subscription performance; and legal obligations for records we must retain. Optional device permissions remain under your control.</p>
  <h2>Sharing and international processing</h2><p>Information is processed by the providers needed to operate purchases, hosting and email support. Providers may process data outside your country, including in the United States. Applicable safeguards, such as standard contractual clauses where required, govern international transfers. We may also disclose information where legally required or necessary to protect legal rights.</p>
  <h2>Retention and security</h2><p>We keep support messages and service records only as long as needed for their purpose, resolving disputes and applicable legal requirements. Purchase records may remain with Apple and RevenueCat to support subscriptions and restoration. Local app settings remain on your device; some purchase identifiers can persist in iOS secure storage. We use reasonable safeguards, but no system can guarantee absolute security.</p>
  <h2>Your choices and rights</h2><p>Depending on your location, you may request access, correction, deletion or a copy of your personal data, or object to or restrict certain processing. Contact us using the email above. Because Mafia has no named account, we may need limited information to locate a purchase record; we will not ask for your Apple password. You may also complain to your local data protection authority, including the CNIL in France. Subscription cancellation and refunds are managed through Apple.</p>
  <h2>Children</h2><p>Mafia is not directed to children under 13. If you believe a child has provided personal information to us, contact us so we can investigate and address it.</p>
  <h2>Policy updates</h2><p>We may update this policy as the app or our practices change. The date above identifies the latest revision.</p>
</MafiaLayout>
